    "result_text": "Patrons now carry shares, and `bin/e2e` passes all 4 tests in the spec.\n\n**What changed:** only `src/main/frontend/src/app/features/people/people.ts`. That's where the patrons cell and the backing were already worked out. The server keeps no backing figure, so it needed no change.\n\n- **Shares:** each person's patrons get 100.00 split equally in the order they were named, each share rounded half to even. The first-named patron also gets the remainder, so three patrons come out as 33.34, 33.33, 33.33.\n- **Patrons cell:** each patron shows as `<name> <share>`, sorted by name, separated by a comma and a space (e.g. `Ben 33.34, Cam 33.33, Dot 33.33`).\n- **Backing:** each patron's settled figures from the last 90 days, times their share divided by 100, added up across the patrons. The calculation is done in exact integers.\n\n**Decisions you may want to check:**\n- **Shares aren't stored.** They depend only on how many patrons a person has and the order they were named, which the existing patron rows already record. So there's no new column or migration. Merging two people keeps each patron row's id, so naming order and shares stay consistent after a merge.\n- **Rounding happens once, on the total.** The request could also mean rounding each patron's part before adding them up, and the two can differ by a cent. The tests pass with rounding the total, but they may not include a case that tells the two apart.",
